      "text": "Advanced Data Management Technologies (IT5PE_CR1) \r\nTeaching Scheme\r\nCourse Code Course Name Contact \r\nHours\r\nCredits\r\nIT5PE_CR1 Advanced Data Management \r\nTechnologies\r\n03 03\r\nExamination and Evaluation Scheme\r\nFormative \r\nAssessment Summative Assessment\r\nISE# MSE ESE Total \r\nMarks Duration Marks Marks Duration \r\n(Hrs.) Marks Duration (Hrs.)\r\n20 CA 20 1 60 2.5 100\r\nCourse Objectives\r\nSr. \r\nNo. Objectives\r\nThe course aims:\r\n1\r\nTo introduce advanced concepts of transaction management and recovery techniques.\r\n2\r\nTo impart knowledge related to query processing and query optimizer phases of a database \r\nmanagement system\r\n3\r\nTo introduce concepts of advanced access control techniques like role based and discretionary \r\nmethods \r\n4\r\nTo introduce advanced database models like distributed databases and emerging data models \r\nlike temporal, mobile and spatial databases. \r\n5\r\nTo introduce the concepts of Big Data technologies and frameworks used to store, process and \r\nanalyze large-scale datasets for strategic decision making.\r\nCourse Outcomes\r\nThe student will be able to:\r\n1\r\nExplain and analyze the concept of a transaction, and evaluate how ACID properties are \r\npreserved during concurrent transactions in a database\r\n2\r\nMeasure and evaluate query costs, and design alternative efficient paths for optimized query \r\nexecution\r\n3 Apply and integrate advanced access control protocols to regulate and secure database usage\r\n4\r\nCreate distributed database models and understand design of applications using advanced \r\nparadigms such as mobile and spatial databases",
