      "text": "5\r\nUnderstand Big Data concepts and explain technologies such as Hadoop, HDFS, MapReduce, \r\nSpark and NoSQL databases used for large-scale data processing and analytics.\r\n3.5 Course Contents\r\nModule Unit Detailed Contents Hours\r\n0.0\r\nPrerequisite\r\nKnowledge of basic concepts of a Relational database, SQL concepts 00\r\n1.0\r\nTransactions Management, Concurrency and Recovery\r\n1.1 Transaction concept, Transaction states, ACID properties, Implementation of \r\natomicity and durability, Concurrent Executions, Serializability, \r\nRecoverability, Implementation of isolation, \r\n08 1.2 Concurrency Control: Lock-based, Time-stamp based, Validation based \r\nprotocols, Deadlock handling, \r\n1.3 Recovery System: Failure Classification, Storage structure, Recovery & \r\natomicity, Log based recovery, Checkpoints, Shadow Paging, ARIES \r\nAlgorithm\r\n2.0\r\nQuery Processing and Optimization\r\n2.1 Operation on Files; Hashing Techniques; Types of indexes: Single-Level \r\nOrdered Indexes; Multilevel Indexes; Dynamic Multilevel Indexes, \r\nOverview of B-Trees and B+Trees; Indexes on Multiple Keys.\r\n08 2.2 Query Processing Overview, Steps of Query Processing, Measures of Query \r\nCost for Selection Operation, Sorting, Join Operation & Other Operations, \r\nEvaluation of Expressions. \r\n2.3 Query Optimization Overview, Transformation of Relational Expressions. \r\nEstimating Statistics of Expression Results, Choice of Evaluation Plans\r\n3.0\r\nData Security\r\n3.1 Advanced Database Access protocols: Discretionary Access Control Based \r\non Granting and Revoking Privileges; \r\n07\r\n3.2 Mandatory Access Control and Role Based Access Control, Remote Database \r\naccess protocol.\r\n3.3 SQL Injection; Introduction to Statistical Database Security, Introduction to \r\nflow control\r\n4.0\r\nDistributed Databases \r\n4.1 Introduction: Distributed Data Processing, What is a Distributed Database \r\nSystem? Design Issues. Distributed DBMS Architecture. Distributed \r\nDatabase Design, Data Fragmentation & Allocation in distributed databases.\r\nOverview of Query Processing and Query Optimization in Distributed \r\nDatabases;\r\n4.2 Overview of Transaction Management in Distributed 08\r\nDatabases; Overview of Concurrency Control and Recovery in \r\nDistributed Databases.\r\n4.3 Overview of Advanced Database models like Mobile databases, Temporal \r\ndatabases, Spatial databases.\r\nIntroduction to Big Data",
